It was further deposed that despite request, all accused persons remained adamant to the demands of car and flat;
State Vs. Harvinder Dalal & Ors. FIR No.201/15 Page no.4 of 22 State vs. Harvinder Dalal & Ors.
that after about 6-7 months, Harvinder alongwith his mother and bhabhi gave beatings to her daughter; that on the birth of female child, all accused persons had taunted her daughter; that in the peelia ceremony, she had given many items despite all of the accused persons again tortured Neetu;
that accused Harvinder never used to give any money from his salary for daily expenditure to his daughter; that in August, 2012, all the accused persons gave merciless beatings to her daughter; that in the month of March, 2014, Neetu was having severe abdomen pain and no one from her in-laws was caring her was not taking her to the doctor; that they had taken Neetu at Max Hospital and there she was operated for stone; that in-laws told her daughter that there is no tradition in the family for sending the daughter to the school; that she had given Rs.50,000/- cash to Neetu for the admission of Bhavika in the school.

Sh. Vinod Gulia (PW-17) is the maternal uncle of deceased, who has deposed that deceased Neetu was daughter of his sister and that he was instrumental in getting them married; that on Sagai, they had given Santro Car and had fulfilled all the ceremonies including giving money etc;
that father of Neetu told him many times about disputes in matrimonial home of Neetu and many times he had gone to house of accused persons in village Ghewra and that when he used to go there,
many times Neetu told him that she used to be harassed in her matrimonial home; that when Neetu gave birth to a daughter, she was taunted by her mother-in-law for giving birth to a girl and that he used to receive telephonic calls from father of Neetu to the State Vs. Harvinder Dalal & Ors.
